  "version": "sft-v2-r22",
  "description": "Round 22's training suite (private mirror; only this manifest is public): sft-v2's records with states of at most 32,768 tokens (Kev-27B tokenizer) in every partition, same order, and at most 500 train records of each of sft-v1's public sources; calibration and development keep only states of at most 8,192 tokens (in-trial screening only); train downsampled further (longify 3,200, tasksource-v1 24,000 records, 0.5 of each sft-v1 synthetic source). Round 22's registration explains these: one epoch and its in-trial scoring have to fit three 8-hour attempts on 8 H200s.",
  "derived_from": {
    "suite": "evals/sft-v2",
    "manifest": "evals/sft-v2/manifest.json",
    "rule": "keep every record whose state (the <state> token + the rendered state) has at most 32768 tokens; of each sft-v1 public source's train records keep the 500 with the smallest sha256('sft-v2-assemble-20260926:public-cap:' + record digest); calibration and development keep only states of at most 8192 tokens; then at most 3200 train records of longify (the smallest sha256('sft-v2-assemble-20260926:keep:longify:' + record digest)); then at most 24000 train records of tasksource-v1 (the smallest sha256('sft-v2-assemble-20260926:keep:tasksource-v1:' + record digest), stratified by family); then round(n x 0.5) train records of each sft-v1 synthetic source (the smallest sha256('sft-v2-assemble-20260926:keep:<source>:' + record digest))"
  },
  "screening_partitions": "calibration and development hold only states of at most 8,192 tokens: they are in-distribution screening partitions (held-out items of the training components; kev.experiment's in-trial temperature and development score), which no round-22 rule criterion reads (every candidate reads transfer-v4 through its own read, and the served temperature comes from the registered held-out-datasets pool), and their longer records took about half of a trial's in-trial scoring time on one GPU",
